## Review fixes for the Marketplace packaging PR (#235)

Context: code review of the Marketplace packaging and first-run setup PR found
a privilege gap on /api/v1 in Apps mode, an incomplete preflight hint, a race in
first-run setup, an unthrottled host lookup, a brittle health check and style
issues. This section fixes them without changing the DAB deploy path.

Changes:

1. src/api/routers/v1.py
   In Apps mode `get_credentials` hands out the service principal only to a
   signed-in admin or app user (the `/api/` prefix skips the role middleware, so
   the role is resolved here with `permission_service.get_user_role`);
   anonymous or no-access callers get a 403.
2. src/back/objects/registry/RegistrySetupService.py
   Preflight now tells the catalog owner to grant USE CATALOG, CREATE SCHEMA and
   MANAGE. `prepare()` creates the schema first and treats a refused
   `GRANT USE CATALOG` as a warning (with the exact statement for the owner)
   instead of aborting; schema grants still run. Reformatted with black.
3. src/back/objects/domain/settings/RegistrySettings.py
   First-run setup holds a process-wide non-blocking lock (second attempt gets
   409) and re-reads the registry location, fresh, before any grant and again
   before Initialize.
4. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseAuth.py
   The `LAKEBASE_*` host lookup now backs off for 60 s after a failure, like the
   endpoint lookup (`_raise_if_backing_off`).
5. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/Bootstrap.py
   `init_status()` reports `schema_missing` (True for a missing schema, via the
   `no_usage` branch or SQLSTATE 3F000 on connect failure). The no-usage message
   moved to `_no_usage_message`.
6. src/shared/fastapi/health.py
   `_lakebase_probe_failure` decides on the `schema_missing` flag instead of
   matching Postgres error text; the permission probe uses it for `no_usage`
   too. Store construction extracted to `_lakebase_registry_store`.
7. marketplace/README.md
   New "Security notes": `apps` scope usage (FEIP-2484 note required before
   listing), /api/v1 service-principal gate, setup lock and USE CATALOG fallback.
8. tests/units/api/test_v1_credentials.py, tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup.py,
   tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup_preflight.py,
   tests/units/auth/test_lakebase_auth_project_resolution.py,
   tests/units/core/test_health.py, tests/units/registry/test_v090_lakebase_bootstrap.py
   Cover the app-access gate, USE CATALOG fallback, setup lock, host back-off and
   the schema_missing flag.
9. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Dropped the Bootstrap.init_status entry (now under budget) and lowered _check_lakebase_permissions.
10. Style
   Ran black over the lines this PR adds (and the PR's new files); unrelated
   lines in existing files keep their current formatting.

